    "classification": "RELEASE_MECHANISM_COMPOSITION_AUTHORITY_SPLIT",
    "summary": "The project required one accumulative candidate, but physical product composition authorization was distributed across Control Plane, B1/B2 locks, historical successor scopes and hardcoded status lists in the guard/workflow. A legitimate new remediation state could therefore make the guard ignore already-authorized product owners and report false source drift. This also made preservation of prior improvements dependent on multiple consumers staying manually synchronized.",
    "demonstratedFailure": {
      "head": "577d455c618fa15614865f4f53832f79f00a210b",
      "guardError": "I6_PRODUCT_SOURCE_DRIFT_OUTSIDE_BOUND_SUCCESSOR",
      "discriminant": "B2 lock authorized the causal owners, but guard b2Active did not recognize status OPEN_PAULA_VISUAL_REJECTED_REMEDIATION_REQUIRED, so the B2 allowed set was omitted.",
      "effect": "The current cumulative source could not be certified even though the causal B2 owners were already physically authorized."
    }
  },
